DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/prime-minister-estonia-2026\n
 \nJoin us for an engaging discussion with Prime Minister of the Republic o
 f Estonia Kristen Michal on:\n\nEstonia at the Front Line: Security\, Resi
 lience\, and Technology: Security\, Europe\, and Technology\n\nEstonia sit
 s at the intersection of some of the defining challenges of our time. Bord
 ering Russia and on NATO’s eastern flank\, Estonia has had to make secur
 ity and resilience a national priority. At the same time\, it has emerged 
 as one of the world’s most digitally advanced societies. For Estonia\, s
 ecurity\, agility and innovation are not abstract ideas -- they are necess
 ities.\n\nIn this conversation with Estonian Prime Minister Kristen Michal
 \, we will explore what it means to lead a country on NATO’s eastern fla
 nk at a time of profound geopolitical change\; why the outcome of Russia
 ’s war against Ukraine will shape Europe and the wider world\; and how E
 urope can take greater responsibility for its own security.\n\nWe will als
 o discuss Estonia’s remarkable evolution into one of the world’s most 
 advanced digital societies\, its ambitions in artificial intelligence\, an
 d what smaller countries can teach us about adapting when new technologies
  are reshaping economies\, governments and societies.\n\n\nThe discussion 
 will be moderated by Michael McFaul\, Ken Olivier and Angela Nomellini Pro
 fessor of International Studies\, Senior Fellow at the Hoover Institution\
 , at the Freeman Spogli Institute for International Studies and at the Woo
